---
import HalftoneStack from '@components/art/HalftoneStack.astro'
import Swoosh from '@components/art/Swoosh.astro'
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b">
  <!--
    Ribbon sweeps the full hero: in at the top right, out at the bottom left,
    where its tail meets the section rule. Sized off the hero's own height
    rather than the viewport — a vw width would reach ~1580px at 1023px, just
    below the `lg` breakpoint — and anchored to the bottom so the tail lands on
    the rule at any width.

    That fixed size is 574.7px, so left-anchored it runs out of window at 559px
    and its cut top-right edge starts showing paper beyond it. From 560 it
    anchors right instead: same artwork, same size, now flush to the window and
    the slack opens on the left where there's nothing to collide with.
  -->
  <Swoosh
    class="pointer-events-none absolute -left-4 bottom-0 h-[125%] w-auto min-[560px]:left-auto min-[560px]:right-0 lg:-right-10 lg:-top-32 lg:bottom-auto lg:left-auto lg:h-auto lg:w-[50rem]"
  />

  <div class="relative min-h-[28rem] px-6 py-10 lg:min-h-0 lg:px-8 lg:py-14">
    <!-- Circles sit alongside the headline at every width, as in the comps. -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] items-start gap-6 lg:gap-12">
      <HalftoneStack class="w-20 shrink-0 sm:w-28 lg:w-40" />

      <div class="min-w-0">
        <!-- Explicit breaks: the comps set this as four short columnar lines. -->
        <!--
          Four steps, because the room the ribbon leaves changes underneath them.

          Below `sm` the ribbon is a fixed size anchored left, so an uncapped
          `11vw` walks the headline straight into it — measured ink against ink,
          clear to ~490px, 5px over at 500, 137px over at 700. 2.875rem is the
          largest cap that still clears everywhere (3rem leaves 8px, because the
          circles step up to `sm:w-28` at 640 and shift the headline 32px right);
          this sits under that.

          From 560 the ribbon anchors right and pulls away, which is what pays
          for the larger `sm` and `md` sizes. Both middle terms are straight
          lines solved from their band edges rather than picked by eye —
          slope `100 × (size₂ − size₁) / (width₂ − width₁)` as the `vw` term,
          offset whatever puts the line through the lower anchor. `md` meets both
          rails exactly, 4.5rem at 768 to 6.5rem at 1024. `sm` is deliberately
          flat over its first 32px, holding 3.3rem until 672 before it climbs.

          `lg` is fixed at 6.5rem, which is where `md` arrives at 1023, so the
          last step is continuous rather than a jump.
        -->
        <h1
          class="display max-w-[11ch] text-[clamp(2.6rem,11vw,2.7rem)] sm:text-[clamp(3.3rem,calc(15vw_-_3rem),4.7rem)] md:text-[clamp(4.5rem,calc(12.5vw_-_1.5rem),6.5rem)] lg:text-[6.5rem]"
        >
          <span class="text-red">Software</span><br />
          for the<br />
          modern<br />
          age.
        </h1>

        <!--
          Left-aligned under the headline from `lg` up, as in the comps. Narrow
          screens hang it off the bottom right instead. Out of flow, so it needs
          the section to hold its own height — that's what the `min-h` on the
          padded wrapper is for, and the offsets here are its padding. Drop the
          min-height and this lands on the headline.
        -->
        <!--
          Shrinks to stay clear of the ribbon on narrow screens.

          Full `.label` size down to ~369px, then shrinks to an 8px floor at
          ~306px. It starts backing off well before it has to: the text only
          actually touches the ribbon at 348px, but easing in early reads as
          deliberate rather than as a last-moment snap.

          To move where shrinking begins, change the `6.7px` — bigger starts it
          wider, smaller starts it narrower. The `4.8vw` is the rate, tuned so
          the text still fits the gap all the way down to the floor.
        -->
        <p
          class="label absolute bottom-2 right-3 text-right text-[clamp(0.5rem,calc(4.8vw_-_6.7px),0.6875rem)] text-blue lg:static lg:mt-7 lg:text-label lg:text-left min-[1024px]:hidden min-[1056px]:block"
        >
          Helpful apps &amp; tools<br />
          For easing complexity<br />
          in the modern world
        </p>

        <p class="label mt-12 hidden text-signal min-[1175px]:block">
          opus_5@xhard:~$ <span class="animate-breathe">just breathe</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p
      class="label mt-10 ml-auto hidden max-w-[47ch] text-right lg:absolute lg:bottom-4 lg:right-4 lg:mt-0 min-[1056px]:block"
    >
      I like my software how I like my coffee:<br />
      Robust, bug free and ethically sourced.&nbsp;
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
